From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:44:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: scale the A53 voltages

Add a station tree on top of the A72 station that lets CPU0-7 and the
CCI follow the vendor's MT6797 operating points with their voltage:

- the DA9214 on the legacy direct-address driver, with BUCKA (VPROC1,
  770-1200 mV) and BUCKB (VPROC2, 800-1200 mV) writable within those
  limits;
- VSRAM_L, coupled to VPROC1 so it stays 10 mV above it;
- full vendor tables, 221-1547 MHz for CPU0-3 and 325-2002 MHz for
  CPU4-7, with VPROC1 as the CPU supply;
- the CCI on the third MCU PLL, 234-988 MHz, following the faster
  cluster through required-opps with the same vendor index;
- capacity-dmips-mhz 740 for the A53s, against 1024 for an A72, as on
  MT8173.

Each point's voltage is the higher of the vendor base table and this
unit's EEM-calibrated value plus the vendor's 62.5 mV cold adder, capped
at 1.2 V. The EEM values were captured from this unit, so this tree is
for this unit. The CCI's 169 MHz point is left out: it is below the
firmware's sync DCM floor of 210 MHz.

Nothing changes a voltage until the regulator, clock and cpufreq modules
load. The energy model's dynamic-power-coefficient is still to be
measured.
